High Density Housing / Commercial - New Building - *****PART 5 DESIGN *** 

To construct a new three storey multiple dwelling building containing three dwelling units with an accessory building and surface parking at the rear providing three parking spaces having vehicular access from the lane

Revision #1 (DPMA:DP-2024-00770) (April 16th , 2025):
1. Peak height increased by 0.06 ft. to 200.77 ft.;
2. Main floor ceiling height increased to 10 ft.;
3. Second floor ceiling height increased to 9 ft.;
4. Foundation plan and crawl space slab elevation revised;
5. Garage revised;
6. Main floor powder room layout and location revised for all 3 units;
7. Unit C main and second floor layout changed;
8. Third floor layout changed and added front & rear deck;
9. Added transparent glazing to front units entrance doors;
10. Added windows at north building elevation/main floor powder rooms;
11. Revised main floor south building elevation by shifting rear landings and stairs while revising proposed windows;
12. Revised main floor west building elevation windows;
13. Revised main floor windows from steel frame with wire glass to vinyl frame with tempered safety glass;
14. Proposed maneuvering at surface parking;
15. Updated impermeability and site coverage calculations and layouts;
16. Revised proposed roof;
17. Revised bicycle space location;
18. Revised unit A north facing window and unit B south facing window at main floor living room;

BRB Review notes:
1. Converting to a strata property
2. Energy requirements per 10.2.1.5
3. Part 5 design
4. Building to be sprinklered to NFPA 13R

High Density Housing / Commercial - New Building - **********PART 5 DESIGN***********
To construct a 3-storey residential building containing a total of three dwelling units, with a detached carport at the rear providing 3 parking spaces having vehicular access from the lane.

******THIS PERMIT HAS BEEN REVIEWED AND ISSUED UNDER THE REQUIREMENTS OF VBBL 2019***********

Building Review Branch Notes:
1. Sch. A, D, Arch. B, Geo. B, Struct. B are submitted. 
2. Entire building is sprinklered to NFPA 13D requirements.
3. All dwelling units have separate exterior entrances.
4. All new windows, doors, and skylights shall conform to AAMA/WDMA/CSA101/I.S.2/A440, NAFS.

Revision #1 related to DP-2025-00465 - June 4th, 2025
- remove attic floor windows on north elevation;
- add gable window addition on north elevation;
- change dormer window size on east and west elevation;
- reduce and relocate skylights;
- remove and add windows on east elevation;
- add tempered glass guardrail on north elevation;
- remove gable wall on north and south elevation;
- adjust main floor powder room of unit C; and
- remove wall for interior and bathroom on attic floor of unit A and B;

Revision #2 No DPMA required. Aug 12th, 2026
- in unit C - Showing the door swing of crawl space access hatch from powder room
- Change of applicant from Deepak Sharma to Johnny (Atul) Sharma, Property Owner.

Field Review - Addition / Alteration - Interior alterations to repair fire and water damage to floors 1 to 3 of this existing hotel at this mixed use building on this site.

Revision #1:
1. To move hallway wall to further renovate all Bathrooms and modify their layouts upgrading plumbing fixtures and barrier free walk-in shower stalls in all levels;
2. To upgrade all electrical and lighting fixtures, fire alarm system, internet, wifi and security systems;
3. To install new flooring and replace all guest room entry doors with 36"wide doors;
4. To reconfigure some guest rooms and entry lobby areas, lower and upper lobby;
5. To renovate existing rear basement areas for Laundry, employee lunch room, and office;
6. To demolish existing bar lounge to become a vacant tenant space for future same use;
7. To provide business center for guest use on first level and browsing area in lower lobby for guest uses, and change of use from part of one hotel suite to retail CRU on the 2nd floor;
8. To add: mech, electrical, and structural drawings to the current fire repair and revision scope of work;
9. To provide entrance to the future bar/lounge from the side of the building;
10. To change the permit Architect of record, CRP, and applicant.

OK for Field Review per D.Holbrook

